  "body": "**Suggestion**\r\n\r\nWhen I register a guest user:\r\n```\r\ncurl -XPOST https://matrix.org/_matrix/client/v3/register?kind=guest -d '{}'\r\n```\r\nand try to connect to a room I get an error `M_CONSENT_NOT_GIVEN` with a given url, but if I follow this url with curl it fails:\r\n```\r\n$ curl -XPOST 'https://matrix.org/_matrix/client/r0/rooms/YYYY:matrix.org/join?access_token=XXXXX -d '{}'\r\n{\"consent_uri\":\"https://matrix-client.matrix.org/_matrix/consent?u=56454643687&h=d7d42ff7c7aca589c334e3c45754547be8514f71b2aacf614847442e74c6ad2d\",\"errcode\":\"M_CONSENT_NOT_GIVEN\",\"error\":\"To continue using the matrix.org homeserver you must review and agree to our terms and conditions at https://matrix-client.matrix.org/_matrix/consent?u=56454643687&h=d7d42ff7c7aca589c334e3c45754547be8514f71b2aacf614847442e74c6ad2d.\"}\r\n[leo@bestos:~]$ curl -XPOST 'https://matrix-client.matrix.org/_matrix/consent?u=56454643687&h=d7d42ff7c7aca589c334e3c45754547be8514f71b2aacf614847442e74c6ad2d' -d '{}'\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=en>\r\n  <head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n    <title>Error 400</title>\r\n  </head>\r\n  <body>\r\n     <p>Missing string query parameter &#x27;v&#x27;</p>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n\r\n```\r\nIf I open this url in my browser or in a `GET` way, I get an html form to fill, but unfortunately I'd prefer to fill this form programmatically (of course, I could parse the HTML, but it's not really a robust method as if the HTML changes, the parser will likely stop working). Would it be possible to provide a way to accept this form purely programmatically? The reason is that I'm writing some \"bots\" that use Matrix to signal WebRTC credentials in a room (to provide fully decentralized P2P communication), and I know my bot will follow the Matrix rules.\r\n",
